# uwsm environment, Hyprland session only — [CHANGE: claude-code | 2026-08-04]
#
# Belt-and-braces duplicate of the `env = AQ_DRM_DEVICES,...` line in hyprland.conf.
#
# Why both: hyprland.conf's `env` is applied by Hyprland itself while it parses its config, which
# is fine, but uwsm builds the session environment BEFORE the compositor is exec'd. Setting it
# here guarantees the variable is present no matter which one wins the race, and it also covers
# anything uwsm starts alongside the compositor.
#
# This file is sourced by uwsm ONLY for the Hyprland session, so it cannot affect the Plasma
# session in any way.
#
# The value is a PCI path, not /dev/dri/card2, because DRM card numbers are enumeration order and
# are not stable across boots. On this machine the NVIDIA dGPU enumerates FIRST (card1), so a
# hardcoded number is actively dangerous here — see hyprland.conf for the full explanation.
export AQ_DRM_DEVICES=/dev/dri/by-path/pci-0000:65:00.0-card
